comments.body:
public rodata ops are coming from https://github.com/google/iree/blob/b154cd99df25272e17bb4cbb29438b70f445028b/iree/compiler/Dialect/VM/Conversion/MemRefToVM/ConvertMemRefToVM.cpp#L107-L109

I can reproduce this bug compiling https://github.com/google/iree/blob/main/iree/test/e2e/models/edge_detection.mlir:

```
symbol conflict: '__constant_3x3x1x1xf32'
target op:
vm.rodata @__constant_3x3x1x1xf32 dense<[-1.000000e+00, 0.000000e+00, 1.000000e+00, -2.000000e+00, 0.000000e+00, 2.000000e+00, -1.000000e+00, 0.000000e+00, 1.000000e+00]> : tensor<9xf32>
  (visibility public)
source op:
vm.rodata @__constant_3x3x1x1xf32 dense<[1.000000e+00, 2.000000e+00, 1.000000e+00, 0.000000e+00, 0.000000e+00, 0.000000e+00, -1.000000e+00, -2.000000e+00, -1.000000e+00]> : tensor<9xf32>
  (visibility public)
ops are *not* equivalent, need to disambiguate
```

I'll work on a fix to the linking pass. This is what I have sketched so far (to handle the general case):
```c++
// Destructively merges |sourceModuleOp| into |targetModuleOp|.
// |targetSymbolMap| is updated with the new symbols.
//
// If a private symbol in |sourceModuleOp| conflicts with another symbol
// (public or private) tracked in |targetSymbolMap|, it will be renamed and
// |privateSymbolOccurrences| will be updated to reflect this.
//
// Fails if a public symbol in |sourceModuleOp| conflicts with another public
// symbol tracked in |targetSymbolMap|.
static LogicalResult mergeModuleInto(
    Operation *sourceModuleOp, Operation *targetModuleOp,
    DenseMap<StringRef, Operation *> &targetSymbolMap,
    llvm::StringMap<unsigned> &privateSymbolOccurrences) {
```

that's modeled after @MaheshRavishankar 's earlier attempt here: https://github.com/MaheshRavishankar/iree/commit/7d3baeb0bd7fa0d8402daf1a3cefee8552a6b8f4

